  <h2>The checklist, in plain English</h2>
  <p class="lede">Every engagement starts with the free 12-point scorecard so you can see the gaps yourself. Then we work the list.</p>
  <div class="svc-grid">
    <div class="svc"><strong>Google Business Profile</strong>Categories, services, hours, photos, description, booking link, posts — and the review link ready to hand to happy customers.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>On-page basics</strong>A real title and description on every page, one clear heading per page, your city and services in the words people search.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Speed &amp; mobile</strong>Compressed images, no bloat, a layout that works one-handed on a phone. Slow sites lose the visitor and the ranking.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Structured data</strong>Machine-readable business info (name, address, phone, hours, services) so Google understands you as a local business, not a blog.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Consistent listings</strong>The same name, address and phone on Google, Apple, Bing, Yelp and the directories that matter — mismatches quietly cost trust.</div>
    <div class="svc"><strong>Measured, not guessed</strong>Search Console and profile insights set up so you can see impressions, clicks and calls — the numbers, not our opinion.</div>
